From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:38:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a8xx: recover even when runtime PM is forbidden

a8xx_recover() resets the GPU by dropping the last runtime PM reference
and waiting for the CX GDSC to collapse. When userspace has written on
to power/control, runtime suspend is forbidden, the final
pm_runtime_put_sync() never suspends the device and recovery logs
"cx gdsc didn't collapse" without resetting anything. The hang then
fires again on the next hangcheck and the GPU never comes back.

Allow runtime PM for the duration of the reset and restore the user's
setting once the GPU is powered again.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750): <to be filled after the g1 --pinned rung>

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
index 038e95327d7..a6bc9a03732 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
@@ -938,6 +938,8 @@ void a8xx_recover(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
 	struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu = to_a6xx_gpu(adreno_gpu);
 	struct a6xx_gmu *gmu = &a6xx_gpu->gmu;
+	struct device *dev = &gpu->pdev->dev;
+	bool rpm_forbidden;
 	int active_submits;
 
 	adreno_dump_info(gpu);
@@ -961,6 +963,17 @@ void a8xx_recover(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 
 	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&gpu->pdev->dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Recovery resets the GPU by letting it runtime-suspend so that the CX
+	 * GDSC collapses. With power/control set to "on" runtime suspend is
+	 * forbidden: the final put below would never suspend the device, CX
+	 * would stay up, the hang would survive and recovery would loop.
+	 * Lift the restriction for the reset and restore it afterwards.
+	 */
+	rpm_forbidden = !dev->power.runtime_auto;
+	if (rpm_forbidden)
+		pm_runtime_allow(dev);
+
 	/* active_submit won't change until we make a submission */
 	mutex_lock(&gpu->active_lock);
 	active_submits = gpu->active_submits;
@@ -994,6 +1007,9 @@ void a8xx_recover(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&gpu->pdev->dev);
 
+	if (rpm_forbidden)
+		pm_runtime_forbid(dev);
+
 	gpu->active_submits = active_submits;
 	mutex_unlock(&gpu->active_lock);
 
